OL,3,ASingaporean man pleads guilty in US to
OL,4,Amassive crypto heist
OL,5,
OL,6,FA Singaporean man pleaded guilty on
OL,7,FTuesday to a racketeering conspiracy
OL,8,Fcharge in the US for organising one of
OL,9,Fthe biggest ever cryptocurrency thefts.
OL,11,FMalone Lam admitted to teaming up with
OL,12,Ffriends to steal $245m (#181m) of
OL,13,Fbitcoin and laundering the proceeds.
OL,15,FThe 22-year-old and his associates used
OL,16,Fthe money to spend up to $500,000 per
OL,17,Fevening at nightclubs, according to the
OL,18,FUS Department of Justice (DOJ). It also
OL,19,Fsaid they bought a fleet of exotic
OL,20,Fcars, ranging in value from $100,000 to
OL,21,F$3.8m.
OL,23,APub: 09-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB  BusinessC Nat TVF  Nat News
